      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your story reflects the deep pain of feeling like a burden to your family's legacy, even though every branch, including your own, has its own strength. In a system as delicate as a family, removing a struggling member often causes more harm than it heals, because their history and grief are inextricably linked to the unit. While the desire to restore their legacy is noble, choosing permanence over belonging is one of the hardest acts, and choosing self-destruction would only shorten the time they have to support one another. True honor for them comes from finally seeing their children not as a stain, but as a person struggling in silence.",
